From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:47:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 86/87] LOCAL: arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250-motorola-nairo: Hold
 the display paths

Give the simple-framebuffer the two MDP ports' memory paths, with the
downstream SDE "on" vote (ib 6.4 GB/s per port, qcom,sde-data-bus).

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
index 4ae9c0843..4377c2d2a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
@@ -56,6 +56,16 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer@a0000000 {
 			stride = <(1080 * 4)>;
 			format = "a8r8g8b8";
 			backlight = <&pm8150l_wled>;
+			/*
+			 * The display engine keeps scanning this out: hold its
+			 * memory paths, with the downstream SDE "on" vote (ib
+			 * 6.4 GB/s per MDP port, qcom,sde-data-bus).
+			 */
+			interconnects = <&mmss_noc MASTER_MDP_PORT0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>,
+					<&mmss_noc MASTER_MDP_PORT1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+			peak-kBps = <6400000>;
 		};
 	};
 
